// Lead sheet with a repeat: the chord row now carries its source barline types
// (|: ... :|, ||, |.) instead of a synthesized plain grid, so a repeated section
// draws real repeat barlines. (Refactor: the same DrawBarlines path as a staff.)
// ⚠️ RE-CUT 2026-08-31 for LYS1034 (a repeat changes the playing order, so it is written
// where the order is — the form). The CLAIM is unchanged and still about the chord row:
// the repeat barlines a form composes reach the row as real barline types, not as a plain
// grid. The row is cut where the old `|:` stood, so the ink is the same book.
title "Repeat"
time 4/4
section Main {
  chords prog { C Am | }
}
section Loop {
  chords prog { F G7 | C | }
}
form main { Main |: ~Loop :| }
score main "lead-sheet-repeat" { chords prog }
